Z||000000||dgroves||12-21-2001||12:27 PM||||I can't find how to put pics up. Am I missing instructions somewhere on the Forum? I've looked in archives...... Is that what the HTML/UBB stuff is for? I'm still having trouble understanding an ECM, hope it ain't too complicated||||reg||9
Z||000001||sqoach||12-21-2001||12:29 PM||||Look at the bottom of this page. There is a little blue and red box (mostly blue) that says 'Pennocks Image Poster'<BR>Click on that and away you go!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>                  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">   <BR><B>86 SE V6 - daily driver</B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||12-21-2001||12:35 PM||||I've used this description before, so it's just a copy n' paste thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>------------------------------------<BR>It's really quite easy (if you have a PC- not a Mac).  First- download "PIP" (Pennock's Image Poster) from this link (or the one at the bottom of your screen):<BR><A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/pip.html" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/pipbutton.gif">   </A><BR>There are instructions there as to how to download the software and set it up properly.  Once finished with the initial setup- it is really quite easy and intuitive: You simply select the pic you want to load using the browse button.  Then click the post button.  Finally, you paste the link (which is automatically pasted to the computer's clipboard when you upload the pic) into your message.  And you're done!  My only warning is to learn about file sizes- I usually don't post any images larger than 5 or 6 inches wide at screen resolution (72pixels per inch).  Anything beyond that can become unbearable to those with dialup connections.||||reg||1
